  "solution": {
    "text": "Rydberg's formula for calculation of wave numbers of lines in hydrogen spectrum is<br/><br/> <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></mrow><mo>̄</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math> <br/><br/>For Balmer series,  <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>  and  <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3,4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></math> , so third line of the Balmer series is due to transition from fifth Bohr orbit to second Bohr orbit."
